From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyuyeong Lee <kyu0.lee@samsung.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:16:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] neutron: fix the health probe for the OVN agent

health-probe.py picks its check from the configuration file name it is
given, and the ovn-agent daemonset passes ovn_agent.ini, which matched
neither sriov_agent.ini nor metadata_agent.ini. The OVN agent therefore
took the RPC branch, which does not apply to it: neutron-ovn-agent runs
no RPC server and consumes no per-agent queue, and reports its liveness
by writing neutron:ovn-neutron-agent-sb-cfg into Chassis_Private in the
OVN southbound database.

The result was not a failing probe but one that never checked anything.
Unlike the dhcp, l3 and l2gw daemonsets, the ovn-agent probe passes no
--agent-queue-name, so test_rpc_liveness() returned success at its
"message bus URL and agent queue name are required" guard. Both probes
are enabled by default, so an agent that stopped answering kept its pod
Ready and was never restarted.

Route ovn_agent.ini to test_socket_liveness(), the check
ovn_metadata_agent.ini already gets, and reorder the branches so the
socket case is matched rather than inferred from the absence of the
others. No configuration change is needed: the check reads
metadata_proxy_socket, which conf.ovn_agent already sets.

This assumes the metadata extension is enabled, which is the chart
default. Deployments running the OVN agent with other extensions only
have no metadata proxy to probe and should disable the probes under
pod.probes.ovn_agent.

The daemonset dates from I3f66ff851e631db3d6de303664564e8942a66cdc,
which reused health-probe.py without adapting it. It matters now that
neutron-ovn-metadata-agent is deprecated since 2025.2 and marked for
removal in 2026.2, so deployments moving to the OVN agent would
otherwise lose the health check the metadata agent had.

Change-Id: I7d940919531125e2806b18fcb6cfe245d6b31450
Signed-off-by: Kyuyeong Lee <kyu0.lee@samsung.com>
(cherry picked from commit e118d9349b8a380d2e1f15b415063800b557290a)
---
 neutron/templates/bin/_health-probe.py.tpl    | 13 +++++++++----
 ...n-agent-health-probe-aad5b735bf150944.yaml | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 releasenotes/notes/neutron-ovn-agent-health-probe-aad5b735bf150944.yaml

diff --git a/neutron/templates/bin/_health-probe.py.tpl b/neutron/templates/bin/_health-probe.py.tpl
index 673261bb0..7774e3ad7 100644
--- a/neutron/templates/bin/_health-probe.py.tpl
+++ b/neutron/templates/bin/_health-probe.py.tpl
@@ -33,6 +33,10 @@ Usage example for Neutron L3 agent:
 Usage example for Neutron metadata agent:
 # python health-probe.py --config-file /etc/neutron/neutron.conf \
 #  --config-file /etc/neutron/metadata_agent.ini
+
+Usage example for the OVN agent with the metadata extension:
+# python health-probe.py --config-file /etc/neutron/neutron.conf \
+#  --config-file /etc/neutron/ovn_agent.ini
 """
 
 import httplib2
@@ -328,11 +332,12 @@ if __name__ == "__main__":
     with open(pidfile, 'w') as f:
         json.dump(data, f)
 
-    if "sriov_agent.ini" in ','.join(sys.argv):
+    argv = ','.join(sys.argv)
+    if "sriov_agent.ini" in argv:
         sriov_readiness_check()
-    elif "metadata_agent.ini" not in ','.join(sys.argv):
-        test_rpc_liveness()
-    else:
+    elif "metadata_agent.ini" in argv or "ovn_agent.ini" in argv:
         test_socket_liveness()
+    else:
+        test_rpc_liveness()
 
     sys.exit(0)  # return success
diff --git a/releasenotes/notes/neutron-ovn-agent-health-probe-aad5b735bf150944.yaml b/releasenotes/notes/neutron-ovn-agent-health-probe-aad5b735bf150944.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..971a60b30
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/neutron-ovn-agent-health-probe-aad5b735bf150944.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    The readiness and liveness probes of the ``neutron-ovn-agent`` daemonset
+    now check the agent instead of always succeeding. ``health-probe.py``
+    selects its check from the configuration file name, and ``ovn_agent.ini``
+    matched neither of the names it knew, so the OVN agent took the RPC branch.
+    That branch does not apply to this agent, which serves no RPC and reports
+    its liveness through the OVN southbound database, and it returned success
+    without checking anything because the daemonset passes no
+    ``--agent-queue-name``. A hung agent kept its pod Ready and was never
+    restarted. ``ovn_agent.ini`` now takes the same unix domain socket check as
+    ``ovn_metadata_agent.ini``.
+
+    The check queries the metadata proxy socket, so it assumes the ``metadata``
+    extension is enabled, as it is by default. Deployments that run the OVN
+    agent with other extensions only should disable the probes under
+    ``pod.probes.ovn_agent``.
+...
